% Generated by hand to match roxygen comments in R/sampler.R.
\name{gp_group_horseshoe_sampler}
\alias{gp_group_horseshoe_sampler}
\title{Gibbs sampler: group horseshoe + GP spectral prior for one node's regression}
\usage{
gp_group_horseshoe_sampler(y, X_s, phi, S_diag, nmc = 3000, burn = 1000, thin = 5)
}
\arguments{
\item{y}{n-vector response (scaled).}

\item{X_s}{n x q matrix of neighbor expressions (scaled).}

\item{phi}{n x m2 GP basis matrix (see \code{\link{build_hsgp_basis}}).}

\item{S_diag}{Length-m2 spectral densities (GP prior variances).}

\item{nmc, burn, thin}{MCMC settings.}
}
\value{
A list with \code{theta_store} (P x saved-iterations), and the
corresponding \code{lambda_store}, \code{tau_store}, \code{sigma_store}.
}
\description{
Fits the regression of one node's (cell type's) expression on its
neighbors, y = Z theta + eps, where each neighbor's coefficient function
is expanded in the HSGP basis, with a group horseshoe prior across
neighbors (for edge sparsity) and a global half-Cauchy shrinkage
parameter, via a Gibbs sampler.
}
\section{Fixes applied when packaging}{

Two bugs in the original script prevented it from running at all and have
been corrected here:
\itemize{
  \item The theta update sampled \code{MASS::mvrnorm(10, ...)} instead of
    \code{MASS::mvrnorm(1, ...)}, producing a vector 10 times too long for
    the very next matrix multiplication to fail on.
  \item The \code{tau_sq} update referenced an undefined \code{global_norm},
    now accumulated as \code{sum_j ||theta_j||^2_\{S^\{-1\}\} / lambda_sq[j]}
    across the neighbor loop, per the full-conditional derivation comment
    in the source.
}
}
